{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/ex-confined-particle-examples","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Example","doco:Section"],"label":"ex:confined-particle-examples","kind":"example","title":"Confined particles across levels: quark to compound","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-confined-particle"],"interprets":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-confined-particle","tags":["confinement","particle","example","levels"],"text":"confined-particle-examples.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<p><a id=\"ex:confined-particle-examples\"></a>\n<strong>Example.</strong> <em>Confined particles across levels: quark to compound</em></p>\n<p><strong>Examples.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><em><code>quark</code>: <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\ell = 0</code>, <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">n_0 = 1</code>, <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">[K]_M = [\\sigma_0]</code> in <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">H_1(q)</code>.</em></li>\n<li><em><code>neutrino</code>: <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\ell = 0</code>, <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">n_0 = 1</code>, <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">[K]_M = [\\mathbf{1}]</code> (unknot <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">0_1</code>, no crossings). Confined and stable at <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q_0</code>; the Frobenius-PSD cone is satisfied since <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\Phi^* = \\mathbf{1} \\succeq 0</code>.</em></li>\n<li><em><code>photon</code>: <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\ell = 0</code>, <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">n_0 = 4</code>, <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">[K]_M = [\\mathbf{1}_{B_4}]</code> (four-strand identity in <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">B_4</code>, no crossings). Confined at <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q_0</code> via the Reeb-bundle holonomy.</em></li>\n<li><em><code>proton</code>: <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\ell = 1</code>, <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">n_0 = 3</code>, <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">[K]_M = [B_3(\\mathrm{uud})]</code> with crossing types <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(pp, pn, pn)</code>.</em></li>\n<li><em><code>neutron</code>: <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\ell = 1</code>, <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">n_0 = 3</code>, <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">[K]_M = [B_3(\\mathrm{udd})]</code>.</em></li>\n<li><em><code>electron</code>: <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\ell = 1</code>, <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">n_0 = 2</code>, <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">[K]_M = [\\sigma_1^3]</code> (trefoil <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">3_1</code>).</em></li>\n<li><em><code>He4</code>: <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\ell = 2</code>, <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">n_0 = 4</code> nucleons, <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">[K]_M</code> determined by the canonical ILP ground-state configuration for <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(Z,N)=(2,2)</code>.</em></li>\n<li><em><code>benzene</code>: <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\ell = 3</code>, <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">n_0 = 6</code> atom-strands.</em></li>\n</ul>\n"}
